  "compactCustomInstructions": "After compaction, immediately re-read plans/session-snapshot.md first if it exists — it is generated fresh from the live transcript and git state at the moment of compaction, so it is more trustworthy than hand-edited files. Fall back to plans/active-context.md only if session-snapshot.md is absent, and treat active-context.md with suspicion if its content conflicts with session-snapshot.md or the verified conversation history — it can carry over stale content from an earlier or unrelated task. Do not waste summary tokens on content already captured in plans/ files (active-context.md, decisions.md, progress.md) — those files persist on disk and will be re-read. Focus the summary on: in-flight tool call results not yet written to disk, ephemeral error messages, and any decisions made verbally that have not been recorded. Always preserve: current branch name, uncommitted file list, active plan file path, and the exact task being worked on at the moment of compaction. Do not re-Read CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or any file they @-import (rules/*.md) after compaction — their content is reloaded automatically as part of the system prompt and a manual re-read wastes tokens on content already in context. Never copy hook advisory text into the summary — exclude [SESSION INIT ...] banners, MANDATORY: graphify-out lines, [STACK HEALTH]/[PLANS HEALTH]/hook: stack-health/hook: plans-health output, and <supermemory-recall>/<supermemory-context> blocks entirely; they are re-injected live by hooks and only compound noise across compaction cycles."
}
